{title: Red River Valley}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}
{tempo: 90}
{difficulty: beginner}
{tags: folk, cowboy}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
From this [G]valley they say you are [D]going
We will [D]miss your bright eyes and sweet [G]smile
For they [G]say you are [G7]taking the [C]sunshine
That has [G]brightened our [D]pathway a [G]while

{start_of_chorus}
Come and [G]sit by my side if you [D]love me
Do not [D]hasten to bid me a[G]dieu
But re[G]member the [G7]Red River [C]Valley
And the [G]one who has [D]loved you so [G]true
